@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "News Letter";
}   
    <style>
        /* General Reset and Body Styling */
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #f0f2f5;
            font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
            color: #333;
            line-height: 1.8;
        }

        /* News Card Container */
        .news-wrapper {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: 50px auto;
            background: #ffffff;
            padding: 60px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
            border-top: 8px solid #c62828; /* Professional Red Accent */
        }

        /* Header Styling */
        .category {
            font-family: 'Arial', sans-serif;
            color: #c62828;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            font-weight: bold;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 2.8rem;
            line-height: 1.2;
            margin: 20px 0;
            color: #1a1a1a;
            font-weight: 800;
        }

        .meta-data {
            font-family: 'Arial', sans-serif;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            color: #777;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
            padding-bottom: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        /* Article Content */
        .article-body p {
            margin-bottom: 25px;
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        /* Drop Cap Effect */
        .first-para::first-letter {
            float: left;
            font-size: 4.5rem;
            line-height: 1;
            font-weight: bold;
            margin-right: 12px;
            color: #1a1a1a;
            font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;
        }

        /* Quote/Highlight Box */
        .quote-section {
            background: #fff8f8;
            border-left: 5px solid #c62828;
            padding: 30px;
            margin: 40px 0;
            font-style: italic;
            font-size: 1.3rem;
        }

        .author-name {
            display: block;
            margin-top: 15px;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-style: normal;
            font-size: 1rem;
            color: #c62828;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        /* Footer */
        .news-footer {
            margin-top: 50px;
            padding-top: 20px;
            border-top: 1px solid #eee;
            font-family: 'Arial', sans-serif;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            color: #666;
            text-align: center;
        }

        /* Responsive Design */
        @@media (max-width: 768px) {
            .news-wrapper { padding: 30px; margin: 20px; }
            h1 { font-size: 2rem; }
        }
    </style>
<body>
    <form id="form1" runat="server">
        <div class="news-wrapper">
            <div class="category">Business & Tech Launch</div>
            <h1>Grand Launch of SRV INDIA Mobile Accessories Company in Mumbai</h1>
            
            <div class="meta-data">
                <strong>Location:</strong> Bhiwandi, Mumbai | 
                <strong>Date:</strong> Monday, 16th February 2026
            </div>

            <article class="article-body">
                <p class="first-para">
                    <strong>MUMBAI (MAHARASHTRA):</strong> The mobile accessories landscape in Mumbai witnessed a significant 
                    expansion this past Sunday with the grand inauguration of <strong>SRV INDIA</strong>. The launch event 
                    attracted a diverse group of prominent citizens, industry traders, and social representatives 
                    who gathered to celebrate this new venture.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The ceremony was marked by traditional <em>Puja-Archna</em> rituals, followed by a ceremonial ribbon-cutting. 
                    The honors were performed by the esteemed saints of the <strong>Shri Swaminarayan Temple, Dombivli</strong>, 
                    adding a spiritual significance to the company's beginning.
                </p>

                <div class="quote-section">
                    "SRV INDIA is built on the pillars of modern technology and trust. Our goal is to provide 
                    the market with high-quality products that consumers can rely on globally."
                    <span class="author-name">— Mr. Ramlal Jangid, Founder</span>
                </div>

                <p>
                    During the address, Directors <strong>Mr. Prakash Jangid</strong> and <strong>Mr. Narpat Jangid</strong> 
                    shared their vision for the future. They emphasized that the company is committed to generating 
                    local employment and contributing to the overall economic growth of the surrounding regions.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The event concluded on a high note, with <strong>Mr. Arjunlal Jangid</strong> and <strong>Mr. Ramlal Jangid</strong> 
                    offering their sincere thanks to all the guests, particularly those who traveled from Surat 
                    to show their support.
                </p>
            </article>

        
        </div>
    </form>
</body>